# Pointu bilingual FR (default) + EN
- Tally.so embed Calendly handles scheduling, WhatsApp handles contact

## Commands

```bash
npm run dev          # start dev server
npm run build        # production build
npm run preview      # preview production build locally
npm run typecheck    # tsc --noEmit
npm run lint         # eslint
```

Always run `npm run typecheck && npm run lint` after a series of changes before considering a task done.

## Project structure

```
src/
 components/       # shared UI components
 sections/         # landing page sections (Hero, Problem, HowItWorks, ForWho, Experts, Pricing, Proof, CTA, Footer)
 i18n/             # translation files: fr.json, en.json
 hooks/            # custom React hooks
 types/            # TypeScript types
 data/             # hardcoded experts list, pricing config
 App.tsx
 main.tsx
```

## Architecture decisions

- Single-page landing with anchor navigation no API calls
- WhatsApp CTA links use `https://wa.me/<number>?text=<encoded>` format
- Calendly embed uses their standard widget script no class components
- ES modules (import/export) no inline styles, no CSS modules
- No `console.log` left in committed code

## i18n rules

- Every user-facing string MUST use `useTranslation` hook add FR key first, then EN equivalent
- If a translation key is missing, i18next falls back to FR

## Component rules

- Keep components under 150 lines they read from i18n and data files directly
- Shared UI components (Button, Badge, Card) accept explicit props with TypeScript interfaces
- Animations: CSS transitions only it filters out unqualified leads. Never soften or remove the disqualification column. The two-column layout ( pas pour vous) must always render clearly on mobile.

## Pricing display

Always show price in both XOF and USD. Conversion rate is defined in `src/data/pricing.ts`. Round USD to nearest dollar use WebP format
- Expert photos: 200x200px max, lazy loaded
- Calendly and Tally scripts: load only when user scrolls to relevant section (IntersectionObserver)
- Lighthouse score target: 90+ on mobile

## Git workflow

- Branch per feature: `feat/hero-section`, `fix/mobile-nav`, `content/fr-translations`
- Never commit directly to `main`
- Commit messages: conventional commits out of scope for MVP
- Do not install animation libraries (Framer Motion, GSAP) Tailwind only
- Do not add a component library (MUI, Chakra, shadcn) always use i18n keys
